 #edb/ref 17592186450686} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ff12093-ab03-562e-bb63-5d8acf007eb3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093b72c3-fff7-5696-aab8-95b8228ec392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450688} {:answer/id #uuid "865d9aa1-0ef9-50e0-9e1c-3bc2b102e74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "865d9aa1-0ef9-50e0-9e1c-3bc2b102e74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450689} :answer-field/id #uuid "1227c816-43e9-5232-8dd5-218cf09ead40" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd839bdc-19bc-52f4-a042-3d3abcdd708c" :question/math-academy-id "q-43778" :question/problem "Consider the vector space ${R}_{3}[t]$ of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $3,$ and its subset $B=\\{p(t)\\in {R}_{3}[t]\\,|\\,p(1)=1\\}.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is closed under polynomial addition\n\n- **II.** $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n\n- **III.** $B$ is a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$\n\n- **IV.** $B$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}_{3}[t]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. For example, if $f(1)=g(1)=1,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1)+g(1) & =1+1 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, if $f(1)=1$ and $k=2,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kf(1) & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not a polynomial from $B.$ So, $B$ is *not* closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $B$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124488 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef65513d-1e9e-571f-8b93-4e2d63aed68e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Subspaces of Function Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b3a3727-45a2-5fb4-95ae-a91e8f4f3239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451353} {:answer/id #uuid "560e913c-ce8a-5991-9d57-1efe0344f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "560e913c-ce8a-5991-9d57-1efe0344f54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451354} :answer-field/id #uuid "7994875a-855a-584f-b0b1-e9adddf96e49" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f71e555b-f6a2-5bfa-a969-f07e226574ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451355} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe4cba6-6e86-5be1-8135-57a663228532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451356}] :answer-field/correct {:a