swer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f90e0f73-a650-56a2-851e-2b406e202da6" :question/math-academy-id "q-47679" :question/problem "Given that that a function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$, has a jump discontinuity at $x=2$, and  is differentiable at $x=3$, which of the following statements must be true for **any** $f(x)$ that satisfy these criteria?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It  is **not** differentiable at $x=2$\n\n- **III.** It is continuous at $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "- Statement I is false. Continuity does not imply differentiability. For example, the function $y=|x-1|$ is continuous but it's not differentiable at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true.  A function that is discontinuous at a point can't be differentiable at this point (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, differentiability implies continuity."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115381 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7586a0dc-25d3-53c5-b3af-cdc314d8fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451411} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc22f55-8ff2-5a8c-bcc3-e6b2be4c1019" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451412}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7586a0dc-25d3-53c5-b3af-cdc314d8fce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451411} :answer-field/id #uuid "f438756f-c79d-53bd-81ac-ca123103d798" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1089274e-1ae2-5b78-a393-34038fd470a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451413} {:answer/id #uuid "501e9e09-32a6-52eb-99c7-4a057e5cb0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "501e9e09-32a6-52eb-99c7-4a057e5cb0bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451414} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ec493f-310f-5901-ae51-8ee0e6d54060" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452554} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be1a7df-639d-50cc-ad8c-bbe0418ffddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451415} {:answer/id #uuid "c045dc4a-dc87-5d60-b5ee-eeb1471cb20e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6be1a7df-639d-50cc-ad8c-bbe0418ffddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451415} :answer-field/id #uuid "51fbc957-ad59-548f-b7b0-b1fa76bed7e9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8298d153-fa1d-58c6-bfcd-efab6041f9f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-47681" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+1, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ 3, & x=1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$\n\n- **III.** It is differentiable on the interval $(-1,2)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement individually. \n\n- Statement I is false.  At $x=1$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}({x}^{3}+1)={1}^{3}+1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x)\\ne f(1)=3,\n$$\n\nand so $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1$ ($f(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=1$).\n\n- Statement II is true. Since  $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=1,$ it is also not differentiable there (because differentiability implies continuity).\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=1,$ it is not differentiable on any interval containing this point. Consequently, it is not differentiable on $(-1,2).$\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7ef1dd-58cc-57f5-9ff9-fc997f4280ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding an Exponential Decay Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2941b1bd-74eb-50ea-8573-ea6bf303ecbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451417} {:answer/id #uuid "3f4809f8-4607-5abc-b8d1-9148e9780cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451418}]