b/id #edb/ref 17592186452558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "182c44b5-94da-5e7b-aa87-a9b6286e7135" :question/math-academy-id "q-47745" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true in relation to the function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** Its domain is $x>0$\n- **II.** Its range is $-\\infty <y<\\infty $\n- **III.** It has a horizontal asymptote $y=0$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of $y=(0.125)^{x}:$\n\n![](images/20/20fae3a813e249a6423567b448a1f5515c3b9127e7c0b82aad541e720db03aca.png)\n\nLet's go through the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ is defined for all input values $x,$ so the domain is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The set of possible outputs of $f(x)=(0.125)^{x}$ consists of all the positive numbers, so the range is $y>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As $x$ increases, the function value gets smaller and smaller, approaching zero. Therefore $y=0$ is a horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x).$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce7ef1dd-58cc-57f5-9ff9-fc997f4280ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding an Exponential Decay Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c4946f-7cfd-5eea-9b2a-3c68b8c04bba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451423} {:answer/id #uuid "631df741-fcdf-5ee9-b554-6ce847f8201f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "631df741-fcdf-5ee9-b554-6ce847f8201f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.